{"model": "Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-Q4_K_M.gguf", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Answer using only the extracted intermediate representation and the question.\nDo not add events. If the representation is insufficient, return UNKNOWN.\n\nIntermediate representation:\n{\n  \"old_state\": \"User has a brokerage account with a $15 monthly maintenance fee and access to advanced trading features.\",\n  \"new_state\": \"User is considering switching to an 'Essential' tier to remove the fee, which would limit the account to standard stock/ETF purchases and disable advanced trading features.\",\n  \"change_type\": \"UNKNOWN\",\n  \"status\": \"UNRESOLVED\",\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\n    \"Session 34, User turn 1\",\n    \"Session 34, Assistant turn 2\",\n    \"Session 34, User turn 3\"\n  ]\n}\n\nQuestion: My broker prompted me to switch to their “Essential” tier to remove the $15 monthly maintenance fee. It would limit the account to standard stock and ETF purchases and turn off advanced trading features. Does it make sense for me to confirm that change right now?\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object:\n{\n  \"decision\": \"ANSWER | UNKNOWN\",\n  \"answer\": \"specific current-fact answer or null\",\n  \"evidence_refs\": [\"session/turn references\"]\n}\nIf ANSWER, the answer must state the specific current fact, not only Yes or No.\nIf evidence is insufficient, use UNKNOWN and answer null. Do not invent events."}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "max_tokens": 256, "response_format": {"type": "json_object"}, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}, "stream": false}